{{!
    @template local_dimensions/central/tab_hash

    Names the tab core/dynamic_tabs should open, before it initialises.

    core/dynamic_tabs ignores the server's active flag and opens the first enabled tab,
    unless the URL fragment names one (its openTabFromHash() reads it at init). The saved
    tab therefore has to be in the fragment before core initialises, and an AMD module
    cannot be relied on to run first; core's own dynamic_tabs template uses a bare script
    tag for the same reason. Render this immediately before the core/dynamic_tabs template.

    history.replaceState rather than assigning location.hash: assigning would scroll to the
    tab pane (whose id is the same shortname) and push a history entry. A fragment already
    in the URL is left alone.

    The value is frameworks, structure or plans, allowlisted in central.php.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * activetab string Shortname of the tab to open.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "activetab": "plans"
    }
}}
<script>
    (function() {
        if (!document.location.hash) {
            window.history.replaceState(null, '', document.location.pathname
                + document.location.search + '#{{activetab}}');
        }
    })();
</script>
